; ---------------------------------------------------------
; VNKit demo script — mechanics tour
;   * backgrounds / characters / music / sfx
;   * choices, variables, conditional branching
;   * MINI-GAME:  @minigame Lockpick → result in $lockResult
;   * EVENT CGs:  @cg — unlocked in the CG gallery (Title → Gallery).
;     RooftopSunset is guaranteed, RooftopNight only on the good end:
;     replaying with different choices is what fills the gallery.
;   * SPINE: add an entry under Spine Characters / Spine CGs on the
;     engine and every "appearance" below becomes an ANIMATION name
;     (Ayame.Smile: plays the "Smile" animation; a CG listed in
;     Spine CGs plays animated instead of static). Without Spine
;     the same names resolve as sprites / placeholders.
; Enable "Use Placeholder Graphics" to run this without any art.
; ---------------------------------------------------------

# Start

@bg Campus time:0.8
@bgm ThemeDay fade:1.5
@set affection=0, lockResult=0, playerName="Alex"

The academy admissions office. A single enrollment form waits on the desk.

; TEXT INPUT — the player signs the form. The name lands in $playerName;
; from now on it can be used in ANY line as {playerName}.
@input var:playerName prompt:"Sign the enrollment form" default:"Alex" max:18

The ink dries. {playerName} — the academy has a new student.

; RICH TEXT works in any line: <b>bold</b>, <i>italic</i>,
; <color=#e8739c>colored</color>, <size=125%>bigger</size> — tags
; survive the typewriter effect intact.
The form notes, in <i>elegant handwriting</i>: <b>"Welcome home, {playerName}."</b>

The form asks for one last detail.

; GENDER BRANCH — no separate files needed. We store PRONOUNS in
; variables and use them later as {he}/{him}/{his}; big scenes can
; still diverge through ordinary @if labels.
@choice "Male" goto:Male | "Female" goto:Female

# Male
@set playerSex="male", he="he", him="him", his="his"
@goto ContinueData

# Female
@set playerSex="female", he="she", him="her", his="her"
@goto ContinueData

# ContinueData
System: Data confirmed. Gender: {playerSex}.

A warm spring afternoon. The school day is finally over.

; ---------------------------------------------------------
; @phoneOn — from now on RMB/Esc open the PHONE menu (before
; this command the classic box menu is used; @phoneOff
; switches back to the classic menu).
@phoneOn
; ---------------------------------------------------------
; PHONE UI 2.11 — messenger hub, like a real messenger.
;
; 1. @msg PRE-FILLS chats: Mom's and Rin's texts are already
;    on the phone when the player opens it (history, not
;    "everyone texting at once"). @msg runs in the background:
;    no forced phone opening, no waiting — a chain of @msg
;    lines all land at once. notify:0 skips the toast banner
;    (backstory shouldn't ping the player).
; 2. @online ... goto:Label brings a contact ONLINE: the chat
;    gets a ● dot, a toast pops up (notify:0 skips it), and
;    the dialogue itself lives under the label, WAITING for
;    the player — lines never advance before the chat opens.
; 3. @waitchat pauses the script until the listed dialogues
;    are finished. The player picks who to talk to first —
;    the live dialogue plays with whoever's chat they enter.
;    remind:"..." — the phrase shown if the player pockets the
;    phone with story dialogues still pending.
; 4. @chatend ends the current dialogue and returns the script
;    to @waitchat, which re-checks who's still pending.
; ---------------------------------------------------------
@msg chat:family notify:0 from:"Mom" "Where are you? Classes are over!"
@msg chat:family notify:0 from:"Mom" "How's your first day, {playerName}? Don't stay out late."
@msg chat:exes notify:0 from:"Rin" "Ayame and I are already on the rooftop 😼"
@msg chat:exes notify:0 from:"Rin" "Hurry up, the sky is unreal today!"
@photo chat:exes notify:0 cg/roof_sky sender:Rin

The phone buzzes. A message from Ayame.

@online chat:ayame contact:"Ayame 🌸" goto:AyameTalk pos:left
@online chat:exes contact:"Rin 🦊" goto:RinTalk notify:0

; The script waits here until the player talks to BOTH: open
; the phone (RMB) to find Mom's and Rin's chats with history,
; a toast from Ayame, and ● online dots for Ayame and Rin —
; the player chooses which chat to enter first.
@waitchat ayame exes remind:"I haven't finished talking to everyone I meant to."
@goto AfterChats

# AyameTalk
Ayame: Heyy, {playerName}! You're coming to the rooftop, right? 👀
{playerName}: On my way.
@typing time:1.4
Ayame: Don't keep us waiting~
Ayame: Btw, look at the sky today!
@photo cg/roof_sky sender:Ayame
{playerName}: Gorgeous. Running up now.
@chatend

# RinTalk
Rin: Finally, {playerName} is online 😼
{playerName}: Gimme a sec, just got to my phone.
Rin: Ayame's been staring at the door non-stop. Get up here.
@chatend

# AfterChats
; @offline clears the online dots and the dialogue queue;
; the conversations themselves stay in the Chats tab.
@offline

You pocket the phone and head upstairs.

@char Ayame.Idle pos:center time:0.5
Ayame: Hey, {playerName}, you actually came! [br]I wasn't sure you would.

; Emotion switch: with a Spine entry for "Ayame" this plays the
; "Smile" ANIMATION mid-scene; with sprites it swaps the sprite.
Ayame.Smile: The view from the rooftop is amazing at this hour.

@char Ayame pos:left time:0.5
@char Rin.Idle pos:right time:0.5
Rin: Oh. You brought someone along.
@sfx Chime

Ayame.Smile: Rin, meet {playerName} — {he}'s the transfer student I told you about.

; The last option appears ONLY for a male player:
; choice conditions support quoted strings (if:playerSex=="male").
@choice "Greet Rin warmly" goto:Warm do:affection+=1 | "Nod quietly" goto:Quiet | "Try the old locker" goto:Locker | "Wink at Rin" goto:Wink if:playerSex=="male"

# Warm
Rin.Smile: ...Hi, {playerName}. Nice to meet you, I guess.
Ayame.Laugh: See? I told you she warms up fast.
@goto Park

# Quiet
Rin: Hm. The quiet type, huh.
Ayame: Give {him} a chance, Rin.
@goto Park

# Wink
@set affection+=1
Rin.Shy: ...Did you just wink at me?
Ayame.Laugh: Careful, {playerName}, {he}'s bolder than {he} looks.
@goto Park

; ---------------------------------------------------------
; MINI-GAME — Skyrim-style lockpicking.
; The engine pauses the script, runs the mini-game and stores
; the outcome in $lockResult (1 = opened, 0 = failed).
; ---------------------------------------------------------
# Locker
Rin: That rusty locker? Be my guest.
@minigame Lockpick difficulty:1 picks:3 var:lockResult
@if lockResult==1 goto:LockerOpen else:LockerShut

# LockerOpen
@sfx Chime
@set affection+=1
Rin.Smile: Huh. It actually opened. Impressive.
Ayame.Laugh: Told you our new friend is full of surprises.
@goto Park

# LockerShut
Rin: Locked tight. Maybe next time.
Ayame.Shy: Don't worry about it. That lock is ancient anyway.
@goto Park

; ---------------------------------------------------------
# Park
@bg Rooftop time:1.2
@stopBgm fade:2

The three of you watch the clouds drift by.

; EVENT CG #1 — always shown, always unlocked in the gallery.
; Add "RooftopSunset" to Spine CGs on the engine to see it ANIMATED.
@cg RooftopSunset fade:1.2
A moment worth remembering.
@cg off fade:0.8

Ayame.Smile: Days like this make everything feel possible.

@if affection>0 goto:GoodEnd else:NormalEnd

; ---------------------------------------------------------
; Good end = a SECOND, missable CG. Save here, then rollback
; (mouse wheel up / PageUp) and pick other choices to compare.
# GoodEnd
@bgm ThemeSunset fade:1
Rin.Smile: You're alright, {playerName}. Come back tomorrow, okay?

; EVENT CG #2 — unlocked only on the good end.
@cg RooftopNight fade:1.2
The city lights flicker on, one by one.
@cg off fade:0.8
@goto Finale

# NormalEnd
Rin: ...See you around, I suppose.
@goto Finale

# Finale
@hideChars time:1.0
And so the day quietly came to an end.[br][br]<i>Gallery, saves, backlog, rollback — everything you just saw is already working. Thanks for trying VNKit!</i>

; SCREEN FADE — @fadeOut darkens the scene (UI stays readable);
; the next script re-opens with @fadeIn. Non-blocking.
@fadeOut time:1.5
@wait 1.6
@goto Epilogue.Start
